          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Magna-grapple" id="3eb0-716b-c779-82ea" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="44ef-dbde-7e89-b898" field="selections" includeChildSelections="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="15" />
              </costs>
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Magna-grapple" id="499e-7334-56b8-7131" hidden="false" typeId="8e6f-7553-28c5-95a0" typeName="Weapons">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Range" typeId="9b9e-0c24-e409-a801">12"</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Str." typeId="1ebc-896c-43de-904a">8</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="AP" typeId="730c-47dc-fdad-3c8b">2</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Type" typeId="1524-30c8-5da7-66ff">Heavy 1</characteristic>
                    <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="45fd-0f50-e1d0-907c">If the Magna-grapple shot hits a vehicle and the target is not destroyed, roll a D6 and add 8 to the score. If the result is lover than the target's highest armour value, nothing happens. If the result is equal to or higher than the target's highest armour value, move the vehicle 2D6" directly towards the Dreadnought.


The target does not change facing and will stop if it comes within 1" or difficult terrain, impassable terrain, another vehicle (friend or foe) or a unit locked in close combat. Teat any non-vehicle unit the target moves over as having been tank-shocked. After the attack, the target will be able to move normally in it's next turn.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </selectionEntry>
